## Two things the re-derivation turned up that I could not have written from memory

The new row carries no `splice_depth` key at all — the refusal precedes the splice. It belongs to neither depth column, so I gave it a third row rather than defaulting it into the tests-only bucket. My first tally script silently did default it, which would have reported tests-only as 36 rows / vacuous 6 and quietly contradicted the published figure. Split correctly, tests-only recomputes to exactly the published 35 rows, classifiable 20, void 10, vacuous 5 — unchanged, as it should be.

The finding is sharper than "Outcome B happened." Both parent files carry a module-level #[cfg(test)], so this commit is inside the READABLE 116 — not a lucky pick from the NONE 100. A commit the --src-census predicate calls readable was still refused, because selection runs upstream of depth. Five sessions of "structurally unmeasurable" now has an address: classify_test_diff_shape, consulted before the splicer is ever reached. Every prerequisite #870 was waiting on was already discharged, and none of them touch it.

